    "answer": {
      "short": "Always true when $a\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "Always true when $a\\ne0$. Splitting the fraction gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a+b}{a}&=\\frac{a}{a}+\\frac{b}{a}\\\\\\frac{a+b}{a}&=1+\\frac{b}{a}.\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $a=0$, both sides are undefined.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
